GENERAL/Service:
-make aixlog sync asynchronous(sync all sink to a dedicated thread)

HTTP:
-http test network negative case(host not found, dns not found, no connection, timeouts)
-ability for http/s server to override nefative handling(route not found, payload too large, etc)
-make http full client(separate connection and request)
-server stops accepting for good after a single async_accept error
 (e.g. EMFILE); re-arm the accept loop on transient errors
-plain HTTP server has no idle/read timeout for keep-alive connections
-clients disconnecting right after the TLS handshake are logged at WARNING
 (Windows reports them as resets); lower to DEBUG

TLS (phases 0-2 done: verified clients, secure server defaults, timeouts; see docs/tls.md):
-phase 3, server features:
  -certificate hot reload: atomically swappable tls::server_context, new
   connections pick up the new certificate, existing ones keep the old one
  -mutual TLS on the server: client_auth none/optional/required + client CA
   in tls::server_config
  -expose TLS details to handlers (req->tls_info(): version, cipher, SNI,
   ALPN, peer certificate subject/SANs/fingerprint, verified flag)
  -SNI multi-certificate virtual hosting (server_config.sni_certs)
  -optional: answer plain HTTP on the HTTPS port with 400 or a redirect
-phase 4, client performance:
  -TLS session resumption cache in tls::client_context (per host:port,
   including TLS 1.3 tickets)
  -connection reuse/pooling is the bigger win (see "make http full client")
-windows: document that a fresh machine only trusts roots already in its
 certificate store (use ca_file for others)

